{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Comedy of Errors"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Go for It!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le10ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future.</br> You use the Future Perfect Continuous tense to talk about an action in the future that is unfinished the time another action in the future starts. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Future Perfect has two forms:</br> <span class=\"italic\">will have</span> + <span class=\"italic\">past participle</span>, or  </br>am/is/are + going to have + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Unlike Simple Future forms, both forms are interchangeable.</br>  </br>Example:</br></br>  <span class=\"italic\">By tomorrow, <span class=\"strong\">we will have forgotten</span> about it. </br>By tomorrow, <span class=\"strong\">we're going to have forgotten</span> about it.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect Continuous</span>, you can sometimes think of it as the Present Perfect Continuous, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.  </br>With the Future Perfect Continuous, an action in the future is unfinished by the time another action in the future starts. It is most often used with an expression of time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:</br> subject+will have been + present participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">I will have been smiling</span> for 48 hours straight by the time you see me on Sunday.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Just think, after tonight,<span class=\"strong\">you will have fallen</span> in love."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By midnight tonight, this whole thing <span class=\"strong\">will have blown over</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By tomorrow, <span class=\"strong\">we will have forgotten </span>all about it."}, {"type": "example", "content": " By Sunday we <span class=\"strong\">will have been laughing </span>about it like it was a distant memory."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I<span class=\"strong\"> will have been talking and carrying </span>on for hours on end. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "By tomorrow, we <span class=\"strong\">will have completely fallen head over heels </span>for each other."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By Sunday, I<span class=\"strong\"> will have been smiling .spear to ear for about 48 hours straight"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Present Real and Unreal Conditionals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The Present Real Conditional is used to talk about what you usually do in real-life situations. The result of the condition is always true according to the initial situation. </br>The Present Unreal Conditional is used to talk about what you generally would do in imaginary situations. The result of the condition is unclear and impossible to predict with certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Present Real Conditional is also called the Zero Conditional. </br>You use the structure:</br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">  If/when</span> ... Simple Present, ... Simple Present</br></span> or <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present ...<span class=\"strong\"> if/when </span>... Simple Present.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Both <span class=\"italic\">if </span>and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> are used in the Present Real Conditional. Using <span class=\"italic\">if</span> suggests that something happens less frequently. Using <span class=\"italic\">when </span>suggests that something happens regularly. </br> Notice that you are thinking about a result that is always true for this condition. You are not thinking about the future or the past, or even the present.</br> Example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> If I go on a date, I usually lower my expectations. </br>When you have a big disappointment, you often get melancholy.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Simple</span> tense to write the zero conditional. The important thing about the zero conditional is that <span class=\"strong\">the condition always has the same result</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Present Unreal Conditional is also called the second Conditional. </br>You use the structure:  </br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span>... Simple Past, ... would+verb </span>or</br> <span class=\"italic\">Would+verb ...<span class=\"strong\"> if </span>... Simple Past</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <span class=\"italic\">If Sally were here, she would be able to give you better advice. </span></br>It is impossible for Sally to be here. The condition is not real.  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">If I were you, I wouldn't get my hopes up. </br></br></span> You use <span class=\"italic\">If I were you ...</span> to give a strong piece of advice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Peter, if I were you, I wouldn't get my hopes up too high. If I go on a date, I usually lower my expectations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you have a big disappointment, you often get melancholy."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If Sally were here, she would be able to give you better advice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If Sally were here, she would have blogged about this as if it were a boxing match."}, {"type": "example", "content": " If you need me, I'll be here."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disenchanted"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "disappointed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am disenchanted with the whole dating process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are disappointed."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "melancholy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a gloomy state of mind"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That song has so much melancholy and sadness."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to calibrate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to determine, check, or rectify"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have calibrated the site on my rifle. Now it is accurate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fret"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to worry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have been fretting about my date for a week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to blow over "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pass over without effect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All your problems will blow over."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall head over heels"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be madly in love"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She fell head over heels in love with him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm ideas for an online article."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a magazine article about online dating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I include quotations from people who are for it and against online dating. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give feedback and take feedback."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, brainstorm ideas for a magazine about online dating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a magazine article about online dating. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include imaginary quotations from people who are for and against online dating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make your article 200 words long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the article with a partner and ask for feedback."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le10ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le10ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Well it's eight o'clock now.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: She will be here. I'm sure of it.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Just think, after tonight, you will have fallen in love.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You think so?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter if I were you, I wouldn't get my hopes up too high. If I go on a date, I usually lower my expectations. That way if the date goes bad, I won't be too disenchanted.\nWhen you have a big disappointment, you often get melancholy. I want you to protect yourself.", "id": 1}, {"time": "28000", "image": "engenn10le10ob09re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: It's cool. I have calibrated my expectations. If things go south, I will be fine.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Really? If Sally were here, she would be able to give you better advice.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: If Sally were here, she would have blogged about this as if it were a boxing match.", "id": 2}, {"time": "43800", "image": "engenn10le10ob09re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: true. Anyway, if it goes sideways, don't fret about it. By midnight tonight, this whole thing will have blown over.\nBy tomorrow, we will have forgotten all about it, and by Sunday we will have been laughing about it like it was a distant memory.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Or by midnight tonight, SWEETGIRL and I will have been talking and carrying on for hours on end. By tomorrow, we will have completely fallen head over heels for each other and by Sunday, I will have been smiling ear to ear for about 48 hours straight.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good luck Peter. If you need me, I'll be here.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You're a good friend.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le10ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le10ob09re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships and use colloquial expressions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I will have been doing and what I will have done."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about connected events and imaginary situations. "